      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research suggests that implementing a Universal Basic Income (UBI) could be a more effective approach in ensuring long-term societal stability. UBI has been shown to reduce poverty rates, improve mental health, and increase economic mobility, as it provides a safety net that can help individuals overcome economic shocks. In contrast, targeted welfare programs often fail to address the root causes of poverty and may be subject to bureaucratic inefficiencies and inequities. Additionally, UBI can incentivize entrepreneurship and innovation, which could lead to long-term economic growth. This approach is supported by data from Finland, Alaska, and Stockton, California.",
